  "answer": "Beacon Insurance is a credible expansion example because its high adoption and measurable business outcomes in Q2 2026 are directly consistent with, and reinforced by, the expansion revenue events recorded for the account in that same quarter.\n\n- **Adoption evidence:** In Q2 2026, KnowledgeHub adoption reached 96.0% and TutorChat reached 92.2%, both exceeding enterprise benchmarks [NL-025#NL-025-S03]. TutorChat average weekly queries rose from 4,200 in Q1 to 6,800 in Q2 [NL-025#NL-025-S03].\n- **Outcome evidence:** New claims adjuster onboarding time dropped from 6.2 weeks to 4.0 weeks [NL-025#NL-025-S04]. Internal support escalations fell by 22%, reclaiming 8 hours per week per supervisor [NL-025#NL-025-S04]. After the April 15 citation validation update, verified queries rose to 94% [NL-025#NL-025-S04].\n- **Recorded Q2 expansion events:** Beacon Insurance generated two Q2 2026 expansion revenue events: $4,500 MRR on 2026-05-15 for multi-department expansion (HR & Legal), and $1,500 MRR on 2026-06-25 for an additional workspace index partition [NL-012#NL-012-S05].\n\nTogether, this shows Beacon did not just promise expansion; it already expanded twice in Q2 while simultaneously demonstrating mature adoption and operational ROI, making it a strong reference for the upcoming WorkflowCoach expansion [NL-025#NL-025-S06].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
